But found it not to be working any longer (maybe because UG is a react app now or received a general makeover with new CSS).
Since I did not find any clue that this has been officially implemented on the page / mobile, I updated the small script so everyone can export their favorites and share on "paper" without having to add the songs to playlist.
I'd still love to see the feature on the page / app, because even though we love UG and use it a lot there a times where we meet "offline" or as in my case want to introduce some polling for the band to be able to share which songs to play next session.
Anyways... here the updated js, it worked for me.
As described in the link above, go to your "My Tabs" page and open any section (like "All"), then open the dev mode of your browser with F12 and paste the script below to your console tab.
Output is still json (I actually only updated the class names to select the correct elements again), but should be easy to transform using standard tools or programatically.
[...document.querySelectorAll('.LQUZJ')].map(item => {
let artistElement = item.querySelector('.aPPf7.jtEAE.lBssT');
let titleElement = item.querySelector('.aPPf7.HT3w5.lBssT');
if (artistElement) {
artist = artistElement.innerText;
}
if (!artist || !titleElement) return;
return {
artist: artist,
title: titleElement.innerText,
link: titleElement.getAttribute('href'),
};
}).filter(item => item)
